  "term": "behavioral couples therapy",
  "definition": "Behavioral couples therapy is a counselling approach that involves both partners together as part of the intervention. In this source, it is used with motivational interviewing to address alcohol use and intimate partner violence, with expected changes in communication and relationship quality.",
